Files (pantheon-files) 7.3.2, two behaviour fixes for a Finder-style column view:

1. No deep count in the overlay bar. Selecting a folder made Files walk its whole
   tree to print "N sub-folders, M files, size"; on a projects folder with millions
   of files that keeps the main loop busy for a long time and swallows clicks.
2. A single click anywhere on a folder's row opens it. Only the icon and the name
   activated; the blank part of the row (most of a 280 px column) only selected.

--- a/src/View/Widgets/OverlayBar.vala
+++ b/src/View/Widgets/OverlayBar.vala
@@ -162,7 +162,6 @@
                     }
                 } else { /* This is a folder. */
                     str = "%s - %s".printf (goffile.info.get_name (), goffile.formated_type);
-                    schedule_deep_count ();
                 }
             } else { /* Multiple selection. */
                 var fsize = format_size (files_size);
